{"version":2,"seriesID":"the-smothers-brothers-comedy-hour-1967","tvmazeID":21694,"title":"The Smothers Brothers Comedy Hour","yearStart":1967,"yearEnd":1969,"overview":"The Smothers Brothers Comedy Hour was an American comedy and variety show television series hosted by the Smothers Brothers and initially airing on CBS from 1967 to 1969. The series was a major success, especially considering it was scheduled against the major NBC television series, Bonanza, with content that appealed to contemporary youth viewership with daring political satire humor and major music acts like Buffalo Springfield, Pete Seeger and The Who. But continual conflicts with network executives over content led to the show being abruptly pulled from the schedule in 1969.","posterURL":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/posters/70659-1.jpg","backdropURL":null,"genres":["Comedy"],"networks":["CBS"],"creator":null,"seasons":[{"seasonNumber":1,"episodes":[{"archiveID":"67-06-04-1-17-vicki-carr-steve-allen-ted-neeley-five","seasonNumber":1,"episodeNumber":17,"title":"19670604.Vikki Carr,Steve Allen,Ted Neeley Five","overview":null,"stillURL":"https://archive.org/download/archivewatch-covers/67-06-04-1-17-vicki-carr-steve-allen-ted-neeley-five.f20aca30.jpg","airDate":"1967-06-04","year":1967,"runtimeSeconds":3600,"videoFile":{"name":"67-06-04 1-17 Vicki Carr, Steve Allen, Ted Neeley Five.mp4","format":"MPEG4","sizeBytes":192422984,"tier":2},"downloadURL":"https://archive.org/download/67-06-04-1-17-vicki-carr-steve-allen-ted-neeley-five/67-06-04%201-17%20Vicki%20Carr%2C%20Steve%20Allen%2C%20Ted%20Neeley%20Five.mp4"}]}],"episodesCount":1,"canonicalEpisodesCount":72,"tvdbID":"70659","artworkSource":"tvdb","cast":[{"name":"Sally Struthers","character":"","order":0,"profilePath":null},{"name":"Lorenzo Music","character":"","order":1,"profilePath":"https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/person/267591/64be9418a4a31.jpg"},{"name":"John Hartford","character":"","order":2,"profilePath":null},{"name":"Spence